{"schemaVersion":2,"sectionID":11021,"chapterID":89,"chapterNumber":"8","sectionNumber":"803.10.6","title":"803.10.6 Clearances.","sourceHTMLPath":"code-sections/mechanical-code/chapters/Chapter 8.html","blocks":[{"id":"11021-html-1","kind":"html","html":"</div><div class=\"clearfix\"></div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-195025\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-195025\"></AnnotationDrawer><div>Connectors shall have a minimum clearance to combustibles in accordance with <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '/codes/newyorkcity/latest/NYCadmin/0-0-0-195024', hash: '#JD_MCTable803.10.6' }}\">Table 803.10.6</Link>. The clearances specified in <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '/codes/newyorkcity/latest/NYCadmin/0-0-0-195024', hash: '#JD_MCTable803.10.6' }}\">Table 803.10.6</Link> apply, except where the listing and labeling of an appliance specifies a different clearance, in which case the labeled clearance shall apply. The clearance to combustibles for connectors shall be reduced only in accordance with Section <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '/codes/newyorkcity/latest/NYCadmin/0-0-0-193089', hash: '#JD_MC308' }}\">308</Link> or via the use of a listed chimney or vent connector system.</div></div><div class=\"clearfix\"></div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-195026\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-195026\"></AnnotationDrawer><div><a name=\"JD_MCTable803.10.6\" id=\"JD_MCTable803.10.6\" title=\"MC Table 803.10.6\"></a><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Table 803.10.6<br></br>Connector Clearances to Combustibles</span></div></div><div class=\"clearfix\"></div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-195027\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-195027\"></AnnotationDrawer><div><ScrollTable><div class=\"xsl-table xsl-table--header\"><table cellSpacing=\"0\" style=\"width: &#10;                  700px&#10;                ;\"><colgroup><col width=\"54.857%&#10;  